msgid ""
"We also define the following utility function, which returns the value of the bit in a bitstring `v` at position `i`. For example, with `v = 6` (binary `110`),\n"
"- `bit_at(6, 1)` returns `0`,\n"
"- `bit_at(6, 2)` returns `1`,\n"
"- `bit_at(6, 3)` returns `1`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This follows the [little-endian convention](/guides/bit-ordering) used in "
"Qiskit: the position `i` is indexed from the least-significant (the "
